From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] python: skip instructionset on riscv64

bindings/python/CMakeLists.txt only builds the `instructionset` nanobind
module (and the AVX2/AVX512 `proxsuite_pywrap_avx2`/`_avx512` variants it
gates) when `CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "(x86)|(X86)|(amd64)|(AMD64)"`,
so none of the three exist in a riscv64 build. But
bindings/python/proxsuite/__init__.py's `_load_main_module()` decides
whether to `from . import instructionset` off an architecture-name
denylist (`arm`, `aarch64`, `power`, `ppc64`, `s390x`, `sparc`) that
predates riscv64 and does not include it, so `platform.machine() ==
"riscv64"` leaves `has_vectorization_instructions` true and the bare
`from . import instructionset` (not inside the `load_module()` try/except
that every other submodule import goes through) raises an unhandled
`ModuleNotFoundError` on `import proxsuite` -- the wheel installs but is
unusable. Add "riscv" to the same denylist the CMake side already keys
off of, so `proxsuite` falls straight through to loading the plain
`proxsuite_pywrap` module, exactly as it does on arm/aarch64 today.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; the identical gap exists in Simple-Robotics/proxsuite's own __init__.py (confirmed against its v0.7.3 tag), so this should go to the original project rather than the cmake-wheel packaging fork, once a riscv64 wheel is public to point at as evidence]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 bindings/python/proxsuite/__init__.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bindings/python/proxsuite/__init__.py b/bindings/python/proxsuite/__init__.py
index 22e5359..8601aac 100644
--- a/bindings/python/proxsuite/__init__.py
+++ b/bindings/python/proxsuite/__init__.py
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@ def _load_main_module():

     machine = platform.machine()
     has_vectorization_instructions = not machine.startswith(
-        ("arm", "aarch64", "power", "ppc64", "s390x", "sparc")
+        ("arm", "aarch64", "power", "ppc64", "s390x", "sparc", "riscv")
     )

     def load_module(main_module_name):
--
2.43.0
